  "purpose": "<p>The Justice Committee examines the policies and spending of the Ministry of Justice (and associated public bodies). This includes courts, legal aid, prisons, probation and the rule of law. It also advises on sentencing guidelines. It cannot consider individual cases.</p>\r\n<p>Follow us on social media: <u><a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/hoccommittees.parliament.uk\">Bluesky</a></u>&nbsp;| <u><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61579513151155\">Facebook</a></u>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<u></u><u><a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/ukcommonscommittees\">Instagram</a></u>&nbsp;| <u><a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/showcase/house-of-commons-committees\">LinkedIn</a></u>&nbsp;| <u><a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/user/UKCommonsCommittees/\">Reddit</a></u>&nbsp;| <u><a href=\"https://x.com/HoCcommitteesUK\">X</a></u>&nbsp;| <u><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLj3mInRJqIekxA--aDW780T_TUCwjea4M\">YouTube</a></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p>Sign up to the weekly <a href=\"https://mailchi.mp/email/committeecorridor\">cross-committee newsletter, ‘Committee Corridor</a>.</p>",
